 2. What happens if a Kubernetes Pod crashes? Will the Service stop working?
 
         "A Kubernetes Service provides a stable network endpoint for accessing Pods. If one Pod crashes,
         the Deployment controller creates a replacement Pod. Kubernetes updates the EndpointSlice 
         with the new Pod IP when it becomes ready. The Service continues routing traffic to eligible healthy Pods without requiring clients to know the new IP address."

